jterm: never read FreeRDP's system-wide certificates.json.

Its "ignore" switch makes FreeRDP accept any server certificate, before the pinned
fingerprints or the helper's callback are consulted. On Windows the file is looked up under
%ProgramData%\<vendor>\<product>\, where every local user may create folders, so one user
of a shared PC could switch off certificate checking for everyone else's jterm. jterm's pin
store is its only certificate policy, so the lookup and its helpers are removed outright.

Applies to the FreeRDP version in ../FREERDP_VERSION; a version bump that moves this code
fails the build at the apply step, and the build scripts then check the result (the string
"deny-userconfig" must be gone from the built library).

